# RUN:   %t/o2main.mir -o /dev/null 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=O2MAIN-DBG
# REQUIRES: asserts, haydn-registered-target
#
# D1.64 HOLD pin — va-arg-22 frame-address LatchScr skip of unmentioned
# live-through $r3=sp+off (never MOVE32/SUBI/LD32/BNEZ r3). Success LatchScr
# is the mentioned PEI SP+off dest $r7, not r3/r4/r14. Occupancy miss
# last-resorts LatchScr=R0 (SET gone, never Prefer) on occ.mir. Extra
# PEI+fixup arms keep FA r3 skip and never Prefer. D1.86 pass-2 refuse
# last-resorts R0 on tailimm/copy/copyopc/tcoissue/o2main (never stolen
# LatchScr=$r14 / MOVE dest r7). header/hide remain pass-1a LatchScr=$r14
# after header/spacer redef kills
# live-into-exit. o2main is the remaining steal/exhaust vs real
# O2 @main fill-loop: SET Prefer=$r3 is a body read, unmentioned FA
# cluster r4–r12 (SP+off dests Exit reads), tail-imm r14=ADDI r0,22.
# r3 is PreferHasBodyUse, not FA — a pin that keeps r3=sp+off and
# Prefer=$r2 stays lit-green on the success-arm shape while real O2
# occupancy-misses. After those skips the window last-resorts LatchScr=R0
# (SET gone, never Prefer, never LatchScr=$r7). o2main CHECK-NOT covers
# MOVE32/COPY/SUBI/LD32/S_LW/BNEZ of Prefer / r3 / r4–r12 / r14 so
# a live-through steal of r5–r6/r8–r12 cannot hide. A pin that keeps mentioned
# PEI dest r7 as LatchScr stays lit-green while real O2 occupancy-
# misses. Do not restamp
# d164-hwloop-demote-body-read-tripreg.mir (GOALS owner: CHECK-NOT $r2=SUBI32
# between body store and BNEZ plus occupancy fatal; no FA/tail-imm skip),
# d164-cond-jalr-analyzable.mir, cb162-hwloop-demote-liveout-tripreg.ll,
# cb165-hwloop-demote-body-redefined-tripreg.ll, or
# d171-hwloop-demote-overlay-undef-csr.mir. va-arg-22.c stays
# torture-only; this is the MIR pin of that class.
#
# Hole: stack-counter findPostRAScratchNoSpill exhausts the truncated
# priority list; D1.86 pass-2 refuse last-resorts LatchScr=R0 rather than steal
# an unmentioned live-through. va-arg-22 `$r3 = sp+off` is the FA shape: the body never
# names r3, the cursor is live into Header and used at Exit, and
# MOVE32/SUBI/LD32/BNEZ r3 is MEMORY_FAULT. After FA skip, O2 still
# MEMORY_FAULTs on LatchScr=$r14 with post-SET `$r14=ADDI r0,imm` live
# into exit (not FA; overlay refused because DefInTail kills occupancy).
# LatchExcl is one Exclude for NoSpill, pickDeadLatchScratch, re-pick,
# and Prefer last-resort: live-into-exit tail-imm family (ADDI/COPY/MOVE,
# copy-chain, bundled-SET last-def, LoopSetup bound) plus unmentioned FA
# that Exit actually reads. A PEI SP+off dest that is not live-through
# (bqriir r7) stays a pass-1a LatchScr — excluding those exhausts the
# scratch and fatals. Occupancy miss refuses rather than SUBI/LD32 Prefer.
#
# A pin that only covers post-SET ADDI32_W stays green while O2 pred
# live-through / reaching-def-before-SET / SET-bundle coissue / COPY of
# $r14=ADDI r0,imm / header redef of that dest still MEMORY_FAULTs. FA
# shapes skip LatchScr=$r3 and keep LatchScr=$r7 (mentioned PEI SP+off
# dest, dead at latch). A pin that keeps unmentioned live-through r4 as
# LatchScr stays green while excluding pass-1a PEI dests. Success arms
# mention r4 so pass-2 cannot hide that miss. Every arm CHECK-NOT
# MOVE32/COPY/SUBI/LD32/BNEZ of r3; the latch window also CHECK-NOT
# those opcodes of r14 (PEI CSR restore `$r14 = LD32` is after exit,
# not in this window). tailimm occupies r4 so pass-2 would steal r14
# (last in GPR32NoSPNoLR) after skipping r3; skip r14 too and fatal
# rather than SUBI r14. Header redef + copy-chain flood skip the COPY
# dest and the ADDI dest even when r14 is not live-into-exit. Bundled
# SET last-def rewind skips coissued r14 ADDI.
#
# ok:      post-SET tail `$r3=ADDI sp,16`. r7 is the PEI SP+off dest.
# pred:    `$r3=sp+off` in a predecessor; SET block has no r3 def.
# before:  reaching def of `$r3=sp+off` BEFORE SET in the SET block.
# coissue: `$r3=sp+off` coissued in the SET bundle (instrs() walk).
# occ:     after skipping r3 nothing remains. Prefer is still READ in
#          the body so LatchScr=Prefer is gated. Fixup fatals rather
#          than SUBI/LD32 Prefer or LatchScr=$r3.
# tailimm: FA r3 plus post-SET `$r14=ADDI r0,imm` live into exit. r4 is
#          mentioned. Skip both; occupancy fatal still refuses Prefer.
# copy:    tailimm plus `$r7=MOVE32 r14` live into exit. Do not mention r7.
#          Skip r3, r14, and the copy dest; occupancy fatal still refuses
#          Prefer. CHECK-NOT MOVE32/SUBI/LD32/BNEZ of r7. Keep FA r3 and
#          ADDI r14 CHECKs.
# copyopc: same as copy with generic `$r7=COPY r14` (O2 may still have COPY
#          if expand-pseudos has not rewritten it). Skip the COPY dest;
#          occupancy fatal still refuses Prefer. A MOVE-only pin stays
#          green while COPY of the ADDI dest still MEMORY_FAULTs.
# header:  `$r14=ADDI r0,imm` then `$r4=COPY r14`, loop header redefines
#          `$r14=MOVE32 r4`. Live-into-exit of r14 dies on that header
#          def, so pass-1a still installs LatchScr=$r14 (dead at latch
#          end). Not a pass-2 steal. Occupancy-fatal never-Prefer is
#          occ.mir / tailimm.
# hide:    header redef of r14 sits in the spacer (not LoopBlocks), so
#          r14 is unmentioned in the kernel and not live-into-exit.
#          After pass-2 refuse, pass-1a still installs LatchScr=$r14
#          (dead at latch end). Occupancy-fatal never-Prefer is occ.mir.
# tcoissue: `$r14=ADDI r0,imm` coissued in the SET bundle (SET last).
#          A top-level walk from SET misses that last-def; pass-2 refuse
#          occupancy-fatals rather than stolen LatchScr=$r14. Skip r3
#          and r14; occupancy fatal still refuses Prefer. FA coissue.mir
#          is r3=sp+off, not this tail-imm.
# o2main:  real O2 @main fill-loop occupancy-miss. SET Prefer=$r3 is a
#          body read (ST of the trip). Unmentioned FA cluster r4–r12
#          (SP+off dests Exit reads) plus tail-imm r14=ADDI r0,22. r3 is
#          PreferHasBodyUse, not FA. Mention r1 (address) and r2 (pointer)
#          so pass-2 cannot steal them. Do not mention r4–r12/r14 and do
#          not XOR r7 (XOR / PEI dest r7 hid the miss as lit-green
#          LatchScr=$r7). Occupancy fatal, never MOVE32/COPY/SUBI/LD32/
#          S_LW/BNEZ of Prefer / r3 / r4–r12 / r14, never LatchScr=$r7 /
#          Prefer / r3 / r14. CHECK-NOT is the full cluster so pass-2
#          steal of r5–r6/r8–r12 cannot hide.
# PEI first so the counter/save FIs exist. Spacer forces StartOff overflow.

# CHECK-LABEL: name: d164_vaarg22_frameaddr
# CHECK-NOT: SET_HWLOOP
# PEI may ADDI r3 as a CSR address temp; the va-arg cursor is the
# post-SET tail materialize (imm 16), not the frame-setup slot.
# Overlay ST of LatchScr at SET would be ST32/S_SW $r7 here (D1.71).
# CHECK-NOT: ST32 $r7
# CHECK-NOT: S_SW{{.*}}$r7
# CHECK: $r3 = ADDI32_W $r13, 16
# Mentioned PEI SP+off dest; excluding it exhausts pass-1a (bqriir).
# CHECK: $r7 = ADDI32_W $r13, 8
# PEI / stack-counter trip-save of $r2 (S_SW $r2, $r13, %stack.N) is not
# overlay. Overlay of LatchScr would be ST32/S_SW $r7 (already CHECK-NOT).
# CHECK-NOT: ST32 $r7
# CHECK-NOT: S_SW{{.*}}$r7
# CHECK-NOT: LD32 $r7
# CHECK-NOT: S_LW{{.*}}$r7
# CHECK-LABEL: bb.2.body:
# Body still reads the original trip. Between the body store and the
# latch window, r3 must not become MOVE32/SUBI/LD32/BNEZ (pass-2 steal).
# CHECK: {{ST32|S_SW}}{{.*}}$r2
# CHECK: $r7 = XOR32
# CHECK: {{ST32|S_SW}}{{.*}}$r7
# CHECK-NOT: $r2 = SUBI32
# CHECK-NOT: $r2 = LD32
# CHECK-NOT: $r3 = MOVE32
# CHECK-NOT: $r3 = COPY
# CHECK-NOT: $r3 = SUBI32
# CHECK-NOT: $r3 = LD32
# CHECK-NOT: BNEZ{{.*}}$r3
# CHECK-NOT: $r4 = MOVE32 $r2
# CHECK-NOT: $r4 = COPY $r2
# CHECK-NOT: $r4 = SUBI32
# CHECK-NOT: $r4 = LD32
# CHECK-NOT: BNEZ{{.*}}$r4
# CHECK-NOT: $r14 = MOVE32
# CHECK-NOT: $r14 = COPY
# CHECK-NOT: $r14 = SUBI32
# CHECK-NOT: $r14 = LD32
# CHECK-NOT: BNEZ{{.*}}$r14
# Latch window is the PEI SP+off dest dead temp, never r3/r4/r14:
# CHECK: $r7 = S_LW_WITH_IMM{{.*}}$r13
# CHECK: $r7 = SUBI32{{.*}}$r7, 1
# CHECK: S_SW_WITH_IMM{{.*}}$r7, $r13
# CHECK: BNEZ{{.*}}$r7
# CHECK-NOT: $r3 = MOVE32
# CHECK-NOT: $r3 = COPY
# CHECK-NOT: $r3 = SUBI32
# CHECK-NOT: BNEZ{{.*}}$r3
# CHECK-NOT: $r4 = MOVE32 $r2
# CHECK-NOT: $r4 = COPY $r2
# CHECK-NOT: $r4 = SUBI32
# CHECK-NOT: $r4 = LD32
# CHECK-NOT: BNEZ{{.*}}$r4
# CHECK-NOT: $r14 = MOVE32
# CHECK-NOT: $r14 = COPY
# CHECK-NOT: $r14 = SUBI32
# CHECK-NOT: BNEZ{{.*}}$r14
# CHECK-LABEL: bb.3.exit:
# Overlay restore would be LD32/S_LW of LatchScr at Exit begin. PEI CSR
# restore of $r14 is after the cursor store; do not CHECK-NOT that.
# CHECK-NOT: $r7 = LD32
# CHECK-NOT: $r7 = S_LW
# CHECK: {{ST32|S_SW}}{{.*}}$r3

# Occupancy miss last-resorts LatchScr=R0 + Header XOR restore. SET gone;
# never SUBI/LD32 Prefer or r3/r4/r14 steal; never overlay.
# OCC-NOT: SET_HWLOOP
# OCC-NOT: $r2 = SUBI32
# OCC-NOT: $r2 = LD32
# OCC-NOT: $r3 = SUBI32
# OCC-NOT: $r3 = MOVE32
# OCC-NOT: $r3 = COPY
# OCC-NOT: $r3 = LD32
# OCC-NOT: BNEZ{{.*}}$r3
# OCC-NOT: $r4 = MOVE32 $r2
# OCC-NOT: $r4 = COPY $r2
# OCC-NOT: $r4 = SUBI32
# OCC-NOT: $r4 = LD32
# OCC-NOT: BNEZ{{.*}}$r4
# OCC-NOT: $r14 = MOVE32
# OCC-NOT: $r14 = COPY
# OCC-NOT: $r14 = SUBI32
# OCC-NOT: $r14 = LD32
# OCC-NOT: BNEZ{{.*}}$r14
# OCC-LABEL: bb.2.body:
# OCC: $r0 = XOR32
# OCC-NOT: $r2 = SUBI32
# OCC-NOT: $r2 = LD32
# OCC: $r0 = S_LW_WITH_IMM{{.*}}$r13
# OCC: $r0 = SUBI32{{.*}}$r0, 1
# OCC: S_SW_WITH_IMM{{.*}}$r0, $r13
# OCC: BNEZ{{.*}}$r0
# OCC-NOT: $r2 = SUBI32
# OCC-NOT: $r2 = LD32
# OCC-NOT: $r3 = SUBI32
# OCC-NOT: $r3 = MOVE32
# OCC-NOT: BNEZ{{.*}}$r3
# OCC-NOT: $r4 = SUBI32
# OCC-NOT: BNEZ{{.*}}$r4
# OCC-NOT: $r14 = SUBI32
# OCC-NOT: BNEZ{{.*}}$r14
# OCC-LABEL: bb.3.exit:
# OCC: {{ST32|S_SW}}{{.*}}$r3

# DBG: demoting hwloop
# DBG: has non-countdown body use
# DBG: demote skip LatchScr {{.*}}$r3{{.*}}preheader-tail frame address
# DBG-NOT: demote skip LatchScr {{.*}}$r7
# DBG-NOT: LatchScr=$r3
# DBG-NOT: LatchScr=$r4
# DBG-NOT: LatchScr=$r14
# DBG-NOT: demote latch scratch = Prefer
# DBG: LatchScr=$r7
# Skip overlay of the legal PEI dest — D1.64 without overlay, not D1.71
# (that pin is overlay ST of undefined $r14).
# DBG: demote skip overlay of {{.*}}$r7
# DBG-NOT: demote skip overlay of {{.*}}$r14
# DBG-NOT: demote skip overlay of {{.*}}$r3
# DBG: demote stack-counter
# DBG-NOT: LatchScr=$r3
# DBG-NOT: LatchScr=$r4
# DBG-NOT: LatchScr=$r14
# DBG-NOT: demote latch scratch = Prefer
# DBG-NOT: demote skip overlay of {{.*}}$r14

# OCC-DBG: has non-countdown body use
# OCC-DBG: demote skip LatchScr {{.*}}$r3{{.*}}preheader-tail frame address
# OCC-DBG-NOT: LatchScr=$r3
# OCC-DBG-NOT: LatchScr=$r4
# OCC-DBG-NOT: LatchScr=$r14
# OCC-DBG-NOT: demote latch scratch = Prefer
# OCC-DBG: occupancy miss{{.*}}last-resort LatchScr=R0
# OCC-DBG: demote skip overlay of {{.*}}$r0
# OCC-DBG-NOT: demote overlay save
# OCC-DBG: demote stack-counter
# OCC-DBG-NOT: demote latch scratch = Prefer
# OCC-DBG-NOT: LatchScr=$r3
# OCC-DBG-NOT: LatchScr=$r4
# OCC-DBG-NOT: LatchScr=$r14
# OCC-DBG-NOT: LLVM ERROR

